                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                        "entry_id": "3fc4dc9c-fb75-3831-9a0f-7b3879398288",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bewitch or enchant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fff6436-a959-45e6-98d6-778cb26fd4d5",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "Not any one of all theſe honord parts / Your Princely happes, and habites that do moue, / And as it were, enſorcell all the hearts / Of Chriſten kings to quarrell for your loue, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72a2ff27-8534-4146-871e-836a29c8fded",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "[H]e called into presence the kazees and the witnesses, and brought in the three Qurundeels, and brought in the first damsel, and her own sister who had been ensorceled, and he married the three to the three Qurundeels, who had informed him that they were kings, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fc36c0f-2d50-45c1-8e1a-3cd9c6f8b09a",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "Juana Maria did not explain why the father had ensorcelled her nephew, though others told me he did it because the nephew had \"damaged\" [\"deflowered\"] the girl and then refused to marry her."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe3f458f-f8c8-46e4-922a-e2a0bddeb497",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "Suroho defended his village by ensorceling enemies who tried to encroach on village land. […] Suroho was accused of ensorceling fellow villagers, and this made him so unpopular that his sons had to find wives in other villages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6973d3a-3ab5-4b49-bcd1-d601fbb8ac2d",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "The woman was obviously a witch. An evil, ungodly creature who would tolerate popery. A foul creature who had lured her husband into his besotted state with her beauty, and probably ensorceled other men as well."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb9d7995-d104-4166-b0e3-be1c5e753261",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "A 52-year-old widower, Mr. A, was referred for a psychiatric evaluation to help in the determination of whether he was competent to stand trial and whether he had mental illness which met criteria for the insanity defense. […] [H]e also believed that she was in a conspiracy with his unnamed enemies to ensorcel him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a11c94b7-ef9e-4e95-a282-acb1347f1806",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "She joked about her previous suspicions of sorcery, saying that one claims one has been ensorcelled, but, really, the sorcery was one's own body."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56e70da2-61c2-48c7-9fc4-fa836f2ff1cb",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "This gentle poem is a model of reader-response theory: the song moulders in the book until the reader, the One Right Reader, ensorcels it, ensouls it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5bdf5ad-f6b0-4957-9ace-4a8471136528",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "Manuel Mestre, for example, suspected Dias of ensorcelling people in the past. She had threatened his sister's children on several occasions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "610f1925-b850-423c-bbed-e4dbdda8316e",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "In Doctor Strange, which ensorcelled the forces of the universe to the tune of $85 million at the box office this weekend, love interest Rachel McAdams is “wasted,” lamented Slate’s Jacob Brogan in his review of the movie. McAdams plays an emergency room doctor, which is pretty cool … but not as cool as the ability to manipulate time, which is among Doctor Strange’s superhero powers—so it’s no wonder Benedict Cumberbatch gets to have all the fun in the movie. Perhaps this will teach McAdams once and for all: Girl, stop playing second fiddle to time-traveling men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f158b25-1e58-487e-bc74-39084d316bdc",
                                "sense_id": "a4ebbf5b-5aa9-343e-b747-6872340520f6",
                                "text": "As they walk on, a world of glass and steel / ensorcels and surrounds them / so even as they move, they never find an exit."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34df8712-346b-3541-9837-5886fad4fcfb",
                        "entry_id": "3fc4dc9c-fb75-3831-9a0f-7b3879398288",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To captivate, entrance, or fascinate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "figuratively",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "312e29ec-26d0-4f6b-8ab6-3ff183cbf7f2",
                                "sense_id": "34df8712-346b-3541-9837-5886fad4fcfb",
                                "text": "[A] distinction is drawn between the man who speaks as a friend and the man who acts like one. Not only might someone fail to live up to his words in deed, but he may ‘ensorcell’ or ‘beguile’ (θέλγοι) a fellow drinker, leading him to believe in friendship that is not supported by his conduct."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1a2f394-9165-4bb8-8abb-70998fdc01de",
                                "sense_id": "34df8712-346b-3541-9837-5886fad4fcfb",
                                "text": "Harry pursed his lips. He thought about Morgan Robertson and his magical books. He thought about Lyle Lillihammer, thoroughly ensorcelled, who was even now starting the second of what would probably be an entire series of PhDs at the SCP Foundation. He thought about Eileen Veiksaar, who had promised with another bewitching closed-mouth smile to meet him for coffee on his first day at Site-43 a month from now. He didn't like coffee, but he did like the possibilities unfolding in front of him. He thought about those possibilities."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ea115f7e-9ffa-4c1a-b5b6-0a9bcf39a02d",
                        "source_entry_id": "3fc4dc9c-fb75-3831-9a0f-7b3879398288",
                        "source_sense_description": "to bewitch or enchant — see also bewitch, enchant",
                        "target_lang_word": "ensorceler",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ensorceler",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a5f4971-b3e5-3a2c-be7d-a9f0c699e329",
                                        "entry_id": "c863f14a-f1bf-32f0-acc6-c0fc0305b670",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Troubler physiquement ou moralement par de prétendus sortilèges."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8d2ea42-184f-4f2c-be7c-de249580d891",
                                                "sense_id": "7a5f4971-b3e5-3a2c-be7d-a9f0c699e329",
                                                "text": "Elle avoua que depuis long-temps, et de concert avec le démon, elle avait pratiqué la magie et les maléfices, qu’elle avait positivement ensorcelé la pauvre madame Lutkens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2607cdf0-d612-3129-ac91-095717b850cc",
                                        "entry_id": "c863f14a-f1bf-32f0-acc6-c0fc0305b670",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Troubler par une violente passion, un amour qui va jusqu’à la folie, jusqu’à la fureur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1abef08-8319-4183-982f-04c53343ca33",
                                                "sense_id": "2607cdf0-d612-3129-ac91-095717b850cc",
                                                "text": "Nous avons appris tout à la fois le funeste destin de Front-de-Bœuf, et ta fuite avec cette belle sorcière juive dont les yeux noirs t’ont ensorcelé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0f3f218-7974-3f44-9249-d6f1d5199e2a",
                                        "entry_id": "c863f14a-f1bf-32f0-acc6-c0fc0305b670",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Captiver."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9346b253-d8b9-406c-8992-491342d1231d",
                                                "sense_id": "c0f3f218-7974-3f44-9249-d6f1d5199e2a",
                                                "text": "Est-ce l’atmosphère de cete ville qui m’ensorcelle?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a3af32c-639d-493e-b7cf-2b8177b7ed27",
                                                "sense_id": "c0f3f218-7974-3f44-9249-d6f1d5199e2a",
                                                "text": "Vous nous ensorcelez, vous enchantez nos sens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d439e72-4710-4c8d-89f7-152ccc42afc6",
                        "source_entry_id": "3fc4dc9c-fb75-3831-9a0f-7b3879398288",
                        "source_sense_description": "to bewitch or enchant — see also bewitch, enchant",
                        "target_lang_word": "hexen",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hexen",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d44bd31-10dc-3e67-a982-6a96427cb5bd",
                                        "entry_id": "12646fbe-1343-3a45-8c5b-dd6295c75cea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "übernatürliche Taten vollbringen, so wie man sie einer Hexe zuschreibt Zauberkunststücke vorführen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "auch realistischer"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f38e5c81-9646-42e2-b83d-c42bb2242cf8",
                                                "sense_id": "7d44bd31-10dc-3e67-a982-6a96427cb5bd",
                                                "text": "„«Hm!» brummte die Hexe auffordernd, tat so, als höre sie zu, fand das Gerede Schnickschnack und überlegte, was es für sie zu hexen gäbe.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "541fba8c-01e8-42ed-9cd2-2a0d0cc00263",
                                                "sense_id": "7d44bd31-10dc-3e67-a982-6a96427cb5bd",
                                                "text": "Diese Frau hext uns noch allen diese neue Seuche an den Hals!"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b9ab1ea-11e9-3e11-916d-06384c72a896",
                                        "entry_id": "12646fbe-1343-3a45-8c5b-dd6295c75cea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "etwas in deutlich kürzerer Zeit zuwege bringen, als erwartet wird"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figurative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57bf956f-27c2-47d8-9e09-ceaf57833952",
                                                "sense_id": "5b9ab1ea-11e9-3e11-916d-06384c72a896",
                                                "text": "So schnell geht das nicht! Glaubst du ich kann hexen?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8d4ffe2-2633-49e1-b158-4279d7479fc4",
                                                "sense_id": "5b9ab1ea-11e9-3e11-916d-06384c72a896",
                                                "text": "Das ging ja wie gehext! Wo hast du den Kalender so schnell aufgetrieben?"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
